tags: memory, ram

The memory of one instance: the RAM of the guest that the processes of the instance
can use at one time. It is a total for the instance, not per core.

The value is in bytes. Example: 268435456 (256 MiB). The memory that the guest kernel
uses for itself is not in the value: the node adds it when it boots the guest. Swap
space is not memory.

An absent value says nothing (it is not 0). Valid in the resources of a container. The
node reserves the value, adds it to the memory of its other instances, keeps the sum
within its capacity, and charges for it. The node can give more than the value (for
example a floor); StartReceipt.reserved gives what it gave.

=== formal
class=resource
measure=the RAM of the guest that the processes of the instance can use at one time, as a total for the instance, not per core; the memory that the guest kernel uses for itself is not counted; swap space is not counted
name=memory
